{"_id":"6a2ff9492204ffbc59e5a751","roadmapSlug":"python-data-analysis","nodeId":"oRaag-FOl50NJM0y4joBm","description":"# Histogram\n\nA histogram groups numeric values into bins and shows the count or frequency of each bin as a bar. It is the primary tool for visualizing the distribution of a single variable: its shape, center, spread, and whether it is skewed or has multiple peaks. `df['col'].hist()` and Matplotlib's `plt.hist()` are the standard ways to create one.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"matplotlib.pyplot.hist","url":"https://matplotlib.org/stable/api/_as_gen/matplotlib.pyplot.hist.html","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb2b"},{"type":"article","title":"Matplotlib Histograms","url":"https://www.w3schools.com/PYTHON/matplotlib_histograms.asp","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb2c"},{"type":"video","title":"Matplotlib histograms in 6 minutes! ≡ƒöö","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2E6fDoz7LuU","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb2d"}],"createdAt":"2026-06-15T13:08:25.799Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:22.099Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e3360acf8c05faf5e1c2a","title":"DataCamp - Data Analyst with Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/QY0dY9"},{"_id":"6a5e3365acf8c05faf5e1ded","title":"DataCamp - Python Data Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/k4V24x"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python-data-analysis/content/oRaag-FOl50NJM0y4joBm.md"}